===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|nl|dum|hêel}}, from {{inh|nl|odt|hēl}}, from {{inh|nl|gmw-pro|*hail}}, from {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*hailaz}}.

====Adjective====
{{nl-adj|heler}}

# [[complete]], [[full]], [[whole]]
#: {{syn|nl|gans|volledig}}
#: {{uxi|nl|Ga je die '''hele''' taart alleen opeten?|Are you going to eat that '''whole'''/'''entire''' cake by yourself?}}
# [[intact]], [[unbroken]], [[undamaged]], [[untarnished]]
#: {{uxi|nl|Ik heb het bord laten vallen, maar hij is nog '''heel'''.|I dropped the plate, but it's still '''intact'''.}}
# {{lb|nl|informal}} [[big]], [[significant]]
#: {{uxi|nl|Dat is een '''hele''' opgave.|That's a '''big''' task.}}

=====Usage notes=====
When the noun is accompanied by a [[definite article]], a [[possessive pronoun]], a [[demonstrative pronoun]], or a [[genitive]] construction, ''heel'' in the sense of "whole" may precede the whole phrase, in uninflected form. For example, the following are both correct:
: {{uxi|nl|de '''hele''' dag / '''heel''' de dag|the '''whole'''/'''entire''' day}}

